        "@type": "text",
        "@id": "copies/zf673fy4620#inscription-text",
        "text": "26525 [heavy mark]  ||  2068",
        "@annotation": {
         "@id": "copies/zf673fy4620#transcription-annotation",
         "belief": {
          "@type": "belief",
          "@id": "copies/zf673fy4620#transcription-belief",
          "certainty": "true",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/zf673fy4620#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded high on the figures of the date: every figure is plain. Stamped, not written. e1 carries five plain stamped figures, 26525, clear of the edge and whole, followed by a heavy over-inked mark. There is no blob before the figures, so the leading-mark trap does not apply here; the heavy mark falls after the last 5 and I cannot make out what it is, possibly a second slug. Read as day, month, two-figure year this is 26.5.25, and no other parse of five figures gives a possible date. The roll number is separate: a pencil 2068 at the edge in e2, matching the printed leader label in e4, 'WELTE-MIGNON. No. 2068 / Poeme / Op. 32, No. 1 / A. Scriabine / Played by A. Scriabine', which itself carries no date. e3 shows perforations only."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
